9	// These tests guard name identity when a lineage document spells code points
10	// with \u escapes. encoding/json accepts a lone surrogate escape and rewrites
11	// it to U+FFFD, which used to collapse two different names into one "�" and
12	// let a bad edge endpoint attach to a real dataset named "�". Every unpaired
13	// surrogate escape must now fail the whole import; matched pairs, the real
14	// replacement character and escaped backslashes stay ordinary, exact names.
